cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use keyaudit, please cite it as below."
title: keyaudit
abstract: >-
  Tests whether panels of model responses can estimate benchmark answer-key error
  rates. They cannot on their own: on MMLU-Pro the panel adds nothing to the human
  relabels (MMLU-Redux), and on 70 real BIG-Bench Hard key defects (20 wrong keys, 50 keys
  that are not the single best answer) its flags catch 2 of them.
  Includes the label-calibrated estimator, a suspect ranking and the identifiability
  limits.
type: software
authors:
  - name: keyaudit contributors
repository-code: "https://github.com/h-a-forster/keyaudit"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.1
keywords:
  - llm evaluation
  - benchmark label errors
  - item response theory
  - prediction-powered inference
